<!--
Label Studio NER Configuration for Resume Annotation
=====================================================
Paste this into: Project Settings → Label Config → Code

Labels and what they cover:
  NAME        — Candidate's full name only (not job titles)
  SKILL       — Technical skills, tools, frameworks, languages, methodologies
  EDUCATION   — Degree name, institution name, field of study
  EXPERIENCE  — Job title, company name, employment period
  DATE        — Standalone dates and date ranges
  LOCATION    — Cities, states, countries (optional — add if you want them)

Annotation rules (read before you start):
  1. ONLY label the entity itself — not surrounding words.
     RIGHT: [Python]SKILL and [React]SKILL
     WRONG: [Python and React]SKILL

  2. Multi-word entities: select ALL words together.
     RIGHT: [New York University]EDUCATION
     WRONG: [New York]EDUCATION  University

  3. Be consistent — if you label "Python" as SKILL in resume 1,
     label it in EVERY resume. Inconsistency hurts the model more
     than having fewer examples.

  4. Job titles go under EXPERIENCE, not NAME.
     RIGHT: [Senior React Developer]EXPERIENCE at [Accenture]EXPERIENCE
     WRONG: [Senior React Developer]NAME

  5. OCR noise — if a word is clearly garbled beyond recognition,
     skip it. Don't label noise.

  6. Name: only the candidate's name at the top of the resume.
     If you're not sure which line is the name, check the email line
     above or below it for context.
-->

<View>
  <Labels name="label" toName="text">
    <Label value="NAME"       background="#2196F3" hotkey="n"/>
    <Label value="SKILL"      background="#4CAF50" hotkey="s"/>
    <Label value="EDUCATION"  background="#FF9800" hotkey="e"/>
    <Label value="EXPERIENCE" background="#9C27B0" hotkey="x"/>
    <Label value="COMPANY"    background="#F44336" hotkey="c"/>
    <Label value="DATE"       background="#795548" hotkey="d"/>
    <Label value="LOCATION"   background="#607D8B" hotkey="l"/>
  </Labels>

  <Text name="text" value="$text" granularity="word"/>
</View>

<!--
Keyboard shortcuts (set above with hotkey=):
  n = NAME
  s = SKILL
  e = EDUCATION
  x = EXPERIENCE
  c = COMPANY
  d = DATE
  l = LOCATION

Workflow per resume:
  1. Read the whole text once to understand the layout
  2. Label the name first (line 1 or 2, usually)
  3. Label all skills (scan the skills section + mention in experience)
  4. Label education entities (degree, institution)
  5. Label experience entities (job title, company, dates)
  6. Submit and move to next

Target per session: 10-15 resumes (about 45-60 minutes)
Total needed before first training run: 50 resumes minimum
-->